{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And Moses said, I will turn aside.</b> From the root סור. If a mem follows it, it means distance, as in סורו ממני (Psalms 6:9) — he says to them, distance yourselves from me. And if אֶל with three vowels follows it, the matter reverses, as in סורו אלי (Judges 4:18) — turn from your place and come to me, that he turns from his place and draws near to the place of the bush." "<b>The great sight.</b> This is the first sign written in the Torah that HaShem performed through His prophet Moses. Therefore He said to him, And this shall be the sign for you that I have sent you (below, verse 12). And Yefet explained this sign, that the enemy is likened to fire and Israel to the bush; therefore it is not consumed."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:31:10.588559575Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}